s":[{"capabilities":{"durably_revivable":true,"historically_viewable":true,"missing_requirements":[],"restartable":true},"commits":[],"dismissed_at":null,"files":{"chat":{"digest":"8c9a54f5ec6747abe25cf8b17f048f8adda7d4d66e6d543775ced3c10c89f8f4","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-p5.1--plan/chat.md","size_bytes":2273},"commits":{"digest":"cca7c9f53b8f548cea73a9c41a40a7c91ac3f835e28b6f8d8f8af5c9bb07c803","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-p5.1--plan/commits.json","size_bytes":89},"embedded_workflows":{"digest":"a398c70160fe308637edd70b38d8cf02cc697183c480675d10f387d529663058","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-p5.1--plan/embedded_workflows.json","size_bytes":80},"meta":{"digest":"b74f52e7481478c2a28288049fa570635377a9464924cabdf58f3adc71806a2c","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-p5.1--plan/meta.json","size_bytes":4905},"prompt":{"digest":"58987a5928bbb4b2c2a61ef82cb17a73ea55bab84de62cb924de454b91211e3e","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-p5.1--plan/prompt.md","size_bytes":169},"state":{"digest":"41158cb18f3814570b41285de216211879314c896ba62e27c649d59d56d2b5da","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-p5.1--plan/state.json","size_bytes":180}},"finished_at":null,"global_name":"bbugyi200.athena.sase-p5.1--plan","local_name":"sase-p5.1--plan","metadata":{"agent_clan":"sase-p5","agent_clan_generation":"20260817185612","agent_session":"sase-p5.1","agent_session_role":"plan","approve":true,"bead_id":"sase-p5.1","changespec_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","cl_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","clan_summary":"[bold #D75FFF]◆ EPIC sase-p5[/bold #D75FFF]\n[dim]  Title: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]Commit finalizer stops failing agents whose work actually landed[/bold #D7AFFF]\n[dim]   Goal: [#D7D7AF][/dim]An agent whose work is committed and pushed is never marked FAILED [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]by the commit finalizer's discarded-work guard. Commit provenance [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]survives conflict resolution, the finalizer decides attribution [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]from evidence the run itself owns rather than from commit-message [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]footers alone, and a concurrent agent's activity in a shared clone [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]can no longer be misread as this agent discarding its work.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim] Counts: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]5[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] phases[dim][/dim] · [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]5[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] waves[/dim]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]plan:202608/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]commit_finalizer_attribution.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim] Prompt: [#87AFFF][/dim]prompts/202608/commit_finalizer_attribution.md[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]sase-p5[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/sase-org/sase--beads/blob/main/pages/sase-p5/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Make the SASE commit footer survive conflict resolution[/bold #D7AFFF]       [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]restamp[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]restamp: verify and re-stamp the run's SASE_* provenance footer onto [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]HEAD during `sase stitch create --resume`, before the push, so a [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]hand-resolved rebase conflict can no longer land the run's own commit [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]unattributed.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Record a run-owned commit ledger[/bold #D7AFFF]                              [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]ledger[dim] · [dim][/dim]after restamp[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]ledger: persist every commit SHA this run created or finalized into the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]agent artifacts directory, including the resume path that currently [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]records a null result, so later stages have positive proof of what the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]run committed.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Decide attribution from run-owned evidence[/bold #D7AFFF]                    [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]guard[dim] · [dim][/dim]after ledger[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]guard: teach the discarded-work guard to consult the run-owned commit [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]ledger before declaring a discard, so a commit the run provably created [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]counts as attributable even when its footer is missing.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Stop blaming an agent for concurrent activity in shared clones[bold black on #FFD75F][/bold #D7AFFF] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]shared[dim] · [dim][/dim]after guard[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]shared: classify foreign-agent and already-published transitions in [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]machine-wide clones as races rather than discards, extending the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]exemption beyond sdd-kind repos and putting the relaxation behind a [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]feature flag.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Actionable diagnostics and regression coverage[/bold #D7AFFF]                [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]hardening[dim] · [dim][/dim]after shared[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]hardening: replace the guard's dead-end failure text with an [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]operator-actionable diagnostic, add end-to-end regressions reproducing [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]both failure clusters, and refresh the affected docs.[/#D7D7AF]","clan_tribe":"epic","epic_bead_id":"sase-p5","llm_provider":"claude","model":"sonnet","patch_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","phase_bead_id":"sase-p5.1","reasoning_effort":"xhigh","role_suffix":"plan","vcs_provider":"GitHub","workflow_name":"sase-p5.1"},"source_run_id":"run-072bbb45327981e6102e1571918adf53","started_at":"2026-08-17T22:56:36.942727+00:00","state":"a